I prefix resume: exact -- a hit resumes only where an idle server's cold prefill of the same prompt starts a chunk (every 2048 tokens) and a prompt's tail snapshot is taken where its last chunk starts, so the hit recomputes the cold run's own chunks and answers bit-identically; a turn re-prefills up to one chunk more than --prefix-resume nearest
