I end-of-request snapshots: on (RADIANCE_EXPERIMENTAL_PREFIX_EORS) -- a decode step whose row completes a position on the 2048-token resume grid past its prompt snapshots the state there, a prompt ending on the grid snapshots its end and every prompt the start of its last chunk, so a conversation's next turn resumes at most 2047 tokens before the reply's last computed position and recomputes the cold run's own chunks from there; such a step is not issued ahead, and the trim after a publish keeps the entries of the chain just published that the request recomputed rather than adopted
I prefix cache: a trunk layer's windowed group is not prefix-cached -- a hit resumes from a window snapshot (a checkpoint slot)
I end-of-request snapshots: on a 16-token grid (RADIANCE_EXPERIMENTAL_DS41_RESUME_GRID) -- a decode step whose row completes a multiple of 16 past its prompt snapshots the state there, and a prompt ending on one its end, so the next turn resumes at most 15 tokens below the reply's last computed position, off the 2048-token chunk grid, and prefills from there in chunks of its own up to the next interval boundary or tail and the cold run's after; exact by DeepSeek-V4.1's partition invariance under large-chunk prefill (a row's bits do not depend on the pass that computes it); such a step is not issued ahead
